Teach proc_reg.h about the Cortex-A53 CPU type, and skip the IORTC wait.

Two separate symptoms, both from the same root cause: XNU keys "which CPU
family am I building for?" on a bare macro that each board header defines
(APPLE_ARM64_ARCH_FAMILY, APPLETYPHOON, BCM2837, VMAPPLE, ...). TISSOT.h
defines TISSOT and MSM8953, which nothing was looking for, so an ARM64
build for tissot fell through to:

    osfmk/arm/proc_reg.h:273:2: error: Incompatible CPU type configured
    osfmk/arm/proc_reg.h:381:2: error: processor not supported

Both are `#error` in the `#else` arm of a dispatch chain. This patch adds
the tissot arm to each chain. The guard uses ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_TISSOT
rather than the bare TISSOT macro because ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_TISSOT comes
from MACHINE_FLAGS in makedefs/MakeInc.def and is therefore defined for
every translation unit, whether or not it includes board_config.h.

Cortex-A53 has 64-byte I- and D-cache lines (ARM Cortex-A53 TRM 6.2), i.e.
1 << 6, which is the same value every other arm64 board uses here.

The IORTC change is not a compile error: IOStartIOKit.cpp waits up to 30
seconds for an "IORTC" service that tissot does not have, because the
exemption was written as `#ifndef BCM2837` instead of a list. Without the
guard every boot stalls for the full timeout before continuing.

--- a/osfmk/arm/proc_reg.h
+++ b/osfmk/arm/proc_reg.h
@@ -253,7 +253,7 @@
 
 #define DFSR_WRITE     0x00000800 /* write data abort fault */
 
-#if defined (ARMA7) || defined (APPLE_ARM64_ARCH_FAMILY) || defined (BCM2837)
+#if defined (ARMA7) || defined (APPLE_ARM64_ARCH_FAMILY) || defined (BCM2837) || defined (ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_TISSOT)
 
 #define TEST_FSR_VMFAULT(status) \
 	(((status) == FSR_PFAULT)     \
@@ -367,6 +367,14 @@
 #define MMU_I_CLINE 6
 
 /* D-Cache. */
+#define MMU_CLINE   6
+
+#elif defined (ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_TISSOT) /* Xiaomi Mi A1, Cortex-A53 */
+
+/* Cortex-A53: both caches have 64-byte lines (ARM Cortex-A53 TRM, 6.2). */
+#define MMU_I_CLINE 6
+
+/* D-Cache. */
 #define MMU_CLINE   6
 
 #elif defined (VMAPPLE)
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@
 	t.tv_nsec = 0;
 
 // RTC is not present on this target
-#ifndef BCM2837
+#if !defined(BCM2837) && !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_TISSOT)
 	IOService::waitForService(
 		IOService::resourceMatching("IORTC"), &t );
 #endif
